Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:42:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: games' videos and sound on FFmpeg (patch 0490)

winegstreamer's Unix side is now FFmpeg (patch 0490): the decoders behind
Media Foundation, DirectShow and DMOs, and the parser behind DirectShow's
splitters, the WM reader and Media Foundation's sources (upstream's
GStreamer byte stream handler). winedmo's demuxer is on FFmpeg too.

tools/build_ffmpeg_ps5.sh builds FFmpeg 8.1.3's LGPL parts with the payload
SDK. build_wine_ps5.sh (--ffmpeg-source) links winedmo.prx and
winegstreamer.prx with it and wine/ps5/pw_ffmpeg_libc.c, the libc functions
FFmpeg needs on the console. The host Wine builds winegstreamer's PE side.
The package carries FFmpeg's licence and names its commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
