diff --git a/wine/patches/0490-winegstreamer-the-unix-side-on-ffmpeg.patch b/wine/patches/0490-winegstreamer-the-unix-side-on-ffmpeg.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..139c3f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/0490-winegstreamer-the-unix-side-on-ffmpeg.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,11479 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: The Unix side on FFmpeg.
+
+Games play their videos through Media Foundation, DirectShow and the WM
+reader, whose decoders (H.264, WMV and VC-1, MPEG-1, AAC, WMA, MP3,
+Indeo) and whose DirectShow splitters and WM reader parser are
+winegstreamer's. Its Unix side was GStreamer, which the console has
+none of, so winegstreamer was not built and every one of them failed.
+
+The PE side stays as it is; its Unix interface (unixlib.h) is now
+implemented on FFmpeg's libavformat, libavcodec, libswscale and
+libswresample, as winedmo already uses them:
+
+- the transform decodes with libavcodec (through libavcodec's parsers
+  where the input may not come in whole frames) and converts with
+  libswscale and libswresample, to the layouts the frontends ask for
+  (plane alignment, 2D buffer strides, display aperture, bottom-up
+  frames); it keeps GStreamer's semantics: pushed samples are held until
+  decoded, MF_E_NOTACCEPTING past the queue length, a stream change
+  before the first frame and on a new size or output format, partial
+  audio reads, timestamps counted from zero for input without them;
+- the parser demuxes with libavformat on a thread of its own, reading
+  through the frontends' read requests as before, queues each enabled
+  stream's packets, and decodes and converts in get_buffer(); streams
+  the frontends know compressed are given as they are when asked to
+  (AVC as a byte stream), the others decoded; seeks are exact unless a
+  key frame is asked for; FFmpeg's own threads log through a buffer a
+  Wine thread empties, since they have no TEB.
+
+Muxing (the MP3 and MPEG-4 sink factories) and the H.264 encoder are not
+part of it and report themselves unsupported. Without FFmpeg
+(HAVE_FFMPEG) the Unix library is built empty, as winedmo's is.
+
+Media Foundation's sources stay with winegstreamer's byte stream
+handler, as upstream has them, now on this parser; winedmo's demuxer,
+also on FFmpeg, takes them with DisableGstByteStreamHandler set, as
+upstream's does.
